    "raw": "First, let's calculate the total cost of the order before any discount is applied. Silvia orders:\n- 2 quiches at $15.00 each, which totals $30.00.\n- 6 croissants at $3.00 each, which totals $18.00.\n- 6 buttermilk biscuits at $2.00 each, which totals $12.00.\n\nAdding these amounts together, the total cost before the discount is:\n\\[ 30.00 + 18.00 + 12.00 = 60.00 \\]\n\nSince the total order is $60.00, which is over $50.00, Silvia qualifies for the 10% discount. The discount amount is:\n\\[ 60.00 \\times 0.10 = 6.00 \\]\n\nSubtracting the discount from the total cost, the final cost of the order is:\n\\[ 60.00 - 6.00 = 54.00 \\]\n\nThus, the final cost of Silvia's order with the discount is $54.00.\n\nFINAL: 54",
